WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.620
Easy Science. Why Does the Moon Change Shape?

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.872
Some nights the moon is a bright, round circle.

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:12.077
On other nights it is a thin line, and sometimes we cannot see it at all.

00:00:12.077 --> 00:00:14.726
But the moon itself does not change.

00:00:14.726 --> 00:00:17.239
It is always a round ball of rock.

00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:19.619
The moon has no light of its own.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.684
It shines only because the sun shines on it.

00:00:22.684 --> 00:00:28.306
The sun always lights one half of the moon, just as it lights one half of the earth.

00:00:28.306 --> 00:00:30.574
The moon travels around the earth.

00:00:30.574 --> 00:00:33.228
One trip takes about four weeks.

00:00:33.228 --> 00:00:37.412
As it moves, we see it from a different side each night.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:42.933
When the moon is on the far side of the earth from the sun, we look at its bright half.

00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:44.629
That is a full moon.

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:50.080
When the moon is between us and the sun, its bright half faces away from us.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.239
We see only the dark side, and the sky looks empty.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:56.112
That is called a new moon.

00:00:56.112 --> 00:01:00.384
On the nights between, we see only part of the bright half.

00:01:00.384 --> 00:01:05.555
So the moon seems to grow for two weeks and then get smaller for two weeks.

00:01:05.555 --> 00:01:10.069
People have used these changes to count time for thousands of years.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:13.778
The word "month" comes from the word "moon."
